From 6c708c55248a7cb9c5cde02caddff0ca5239da30 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: slydlake <sly.dlake@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 14:50:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 02/16] server: stop strings apply to the answer, not to an
 open reasoning block

A request whose rendered prompt ends inside an open <think> block starts its
reply as reasoning, and the caller's stop strings were matched against that
reasoning too. lm-eval's GSM8K stops on "Q:", and a reasoning model
restating the question writes exactly that while thinking: the request ended
after ~25 tokens with no answer at all (empty content), which scores as a
wrong answer.

Stop strings now match only after the block's closer
(Detokenizer::defer_stops_until, the server's own scan from the closer on, and
no stop strings for the scheduler, which cannot tell reasoning from answer).
A prompt that does not open a block (reasoning off, or a closed block)
matches from the first token as before.

Verified: with stop ["Q:","</s>","<|im_end|>"] the GSM8K robe question now
answers "3 bolts" (was empty); a stop string inside the answer still cuts it;
with reasoning_effort none a stop string cuts from the first token.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 core/server/adapters.h  |  1 +
 core/server/iface.h     |  3 +++
 core/server/oai.cpp     |  8 ++++++++
 core/server/oai.h       |  3 +++
 core/server/server.cpp  | 16 ++++++++++++++--
 core/text/tokenizer.cpp | 18 ++++++++++++++++--
 core/text/tokenizer.h   | 11 +++++++++++
 7 files changed, 56 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

