From 0003c68c75d25c2d15390044686463004c836e43 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: slydlake <sly.dlake@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 14:50:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 03/16] qwen35: RADIANCE_GDN_STATE=f16 stores the delta net
 state at half width (opt-in)

RADIANCE_GDN_STATE=f16 declares the delta net's recurrent state as f16 (libr4d
reads the width off the state operand in both GDN decode rows and the chunk
scan). 144 -> 72 MiB a slot, two slots a sequence and the checkpoint a slot
with it: ~1.1 GiB at 8 sequences (~37k KV tokens), the same again if the
checkpoint slots are kept (up to ~55k). Default stays f32; the text changes
slightly (round trip ~5e-4 relative), so it needs KL / acceptance numbers
before it is anybody's default. Unknown values warn and use f32.

Measured (seq8-kv A/B, R9700 at 210 W, 8 sequences): KV 374144 -> 433248 tokens
without giving up checkpoint slots; KL 0.009874 -> 0.009865, top-1 95.09 ->
95.07 %, acceptance -0.6 % greedy (noise), step 33.72 -> 33.55 ms.

docs/GUIDE.md documents the switch in section 8.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
