From 60894dfc09fce477417885269c7937195e6c1020 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: slydlake <sly.dlake@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 14:50:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 04/16] sched: adaptive per-sequence verify length for the
 block drafter (RADIANCE_ADAPTIVE_K)

The block drafter proposes `depth` tokens in one pass, so a shorter verify
prefix per sequence costs the drafter nothing and shrinks the trunk step and
the drafter's context pass: fewer rows through the trunk (M falls, and with it
the decode step), and no position that was going to be rejected is paid for.
Every emitted token is still the target's own choice; only how many draft
tokens a step verifies changes.

- Policy (core/sched/adaptive_k.{h,cpp}): each sequence accepts further draft
  positions with probability q_i (geometric), estimated from its own history
  with censoring (decayed hits / evaluated positions, shrunk toward the pooled
  estimate by `prior` pseudo-positions). The batch picks k_i from a small set
  (default 1,3,5,7) by greedy marginal gain, maximising
  sum E_i(k_i) / T(M) against a step-cost model T(M) = a + b*M (or a measured
  piecewise-linear table). Deterministic, host-only, no allocation after
  configure().
- Quantised on purpose: a recorded pass is keyed by n_tok, max_q_len and
  n_spec, so free per-sequence lengths would thrash the recorded-pass cache.
  The length set bounds max_q_len/n_spec and `quant` restricts the total row
  count to multiples of it (8 sequences, quant 8: at most seven shapes).
- Inactive below `min_rows` total rows (default 32): a single stream or two
  is weight-bound and a draft row is nearly free, so it stays untouched
  (bit-identical output).
- Wiring: scheduler.{h,cpp} cap each sequence's draft for the step being
  planned (SchedReq::ak, ak_cap); the engine enables it for a block drafter
  only (a serial drafter's depth is fixed on the card). Counters in
  SchedMetrics.
- Default off; knobs RADIANCE_ADAPTIVE_K_{LENS,ALPHA,PRIOR,COST_A,COST_B,
  COST_TABLE,MIN_ROWS,QUANT}, documented in GUIDE section 8.

Measured on an R9700, GPTQ-MXFP4 Qwen3.8-27B + DFlash2, 8 concurrent
requests, switch off/on/off/on in one window: c8 with staggered arrivals
390.7 / 372.0 -> 420.6 / 415.9 tok/s (+9.8 %; vLLM 416.5), steady c8 366 -> 387
(+5.7 %); engine step 60.5 -> 51.8 ms, 6.0-6.8 instead of 8 rows per
sequence-step; single stream bit-identical (93.9 tok/s); KL against the
reference unchanged (0.0099, top-1 95.09 %). Policy log: 954 of 2048 steps
shortened, 7.1 rows saved a step.

Tests: sched_test covers the policy (monotonic choice, quantisation, censored
estimate, min_rows, determinism).

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
