From 2bd318d08490ab1ebba2935a4ab13b420f9dc975 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: slydlake <sly.dlake@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 14:50:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 05/16] sched: whole-context lookup draft for block drafters
 (RADIANCE_LOOKUP_DRAFT, default off)

A windowed block drafter (DFlash2: 2048 tokens) cannot see a source further
back, so a far copy, an edit or a re-emitted block drafts at ~3.3 tokens a
step instead of ~7. A per-sequence incremental suffix index over prompt +
output (hash chain over the ng-gram ending at each position, holding only
positions already further back than the drafter window) finds the longest
earlier match (up to 24 tokens, most recent on a tie, bounded chain walk).
An ENTER 8 / STAY 3 / HOT 3 state machine decides per step; when it takes
the step, the drafter proposal is replaced by the continuation of the match.
The decision is taken for every decode-ready sequence without a proposal too,
because a drafter declines a sequence whose draft cache has a hole (every
prefix-cache hit leaves one). The verify is unchanged: lossless.

Interplay with RADIANCE_ADAPTIVE_K: a lookup step keeps its full length and
stays out of the adaptive acceptance estimate.

Knobs RADIANCE_LOOKUP_{DRAFT,ENTER,STAY,HOT,MAX_MATCH,MIN_DIST,CHAIN}
(GUIDE, performance switches). Metrics
radiance:lookup_draft_{taken,steps,tokens,accepted}_total.

Measured (Qwen3.8-27B + DFlash2, 210 W): far copy +31..38 % TG at
8k/32k context, edit +7..11 % at 32k (-3..4 % at 8k), free generation,
summary and short prompts unchanged.

Tests: lookup_draft_test (index equals the exhaustive scan on random text,
window and tie rules, policy transitions, CPU cost at 262k: index build
2 ms, steady search < 1 us mean); sched_test (lossless far copy, edits,
STAY/HOT, 8 sequences beside adaptive-k, 9000-token prompt with a silent
drafter, a real 11042-token Qwen3.5 stream in tests/data/lookup).

tools/rad_tokenize.cpp: text file to token ids with the model tokenizer, CPU
only, for prompt-length checks and for making test fixtures (the
tests/data/lookup streams were made with it).

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
