From 44307c5130075f725700015ccc2d5156df3c21ec Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: slydlake <sly.dlake@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 14:50:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 06/16] sched: draft refill, end a prefix hit a window before
 the prompt so the block drafter has context (RADIANCE_DRAFT_REFILL)

A prefix-cache hit leaves a windowed block drafter (DFlash2) without K/V for
the cached tokens: its own KV group is not prefix-cached, and block_begin
declines the sequence until the window has slid past the hole. In multi-turn
chat that is ~1 token per step on the turn that should benefit most.

RADIANCE_DRAFT_REFILL (default: the drafter window, 0 = off) caps the hit at
prompt_len - refill, at a linear-state checkpoint (PrefixCache::lookup
takes cap_tokens; IPrefixCache::lookup_capped), so the trunk recomputes those
tokens and the drafter context pass covers its window. The whole hit is kept
when no checkpoint is within 2 * refill. Counters
radiance:draft_refills_total and radiance:draft_refill_tokens_total.

Measured (Qwen3.8-27B + DFlash2, multi-turn turn 2 at ~11k context):
1.29 to ~4.0 tokens per step, wall 6.0 to 3.4 s for 256 tokens; cold turns
unchanged. Lossless: only which tokens are recomputed changes.

Tests: sched_test (hit ends a window before the prompt, clamp to the window,
hit already far enough back, no checkpoint near enough, no hit), mem_test
(capped lookup). sched_test Fixture::build takes max_ctx.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
