From 01c5c46aa333230be2fadbc5de2dc78b99f57e7e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: slydlake <sly.dlake@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 14:50:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 07/16] libr4d: int4 logits rows for the lm_head (i4, u4g64,
 u4g128), register-lean tile for M > 16

The lm_head is the widest GEMM of the model (248320 x 5120). At 4 bits it reads
half the bytes of the block-fp8 head. Three rows on lm_wmma_kernel's WMMA tile,
f32 logits out; the weight is staged through LDS at FK/2 + 8 bytes a row, one
block's partial at a time; FKB 4 at MT <= 2, 2 above (R4D_LM4_FKB pins it).

- logits_gemm_i4: symmetric. Row = K/2 bytes of two's-complement nibbles, the
  row's own bf16 scale per 128 in its tail, the 16-byte pad
  (r4d_fp8::lm4_row_bytes). Layout hooks take libquant's
  `codes=i4 group=128 scale=bf16`.
- logits_gemm_u4g64 / _u4g128: the same generalised over the scale group (64
  or 128) and an asymmetric grid, libquant `codes=u4 zero=u8`: unsigned
  nibbles, bf16 scale a group, u8 zero a group, pad (lm4a_row_bytes),
  (code - zero) * scale. Two rows because the op carries no group; each layout
  hook takes only its own.
- nibble trick for the asymmetric tile: 128 + n for a nibble n is exact in
  bf16 with the bits 0x4300 | n, so eight codes become four packed bf16
  pairs with an AND, a shift and an OR each; the offset is taken back per
  group, sum (128 + n) x = sum (n - z) x + (128 + z) sum x, with sum x from one
  more WMMA against a B fragment of ones. No conversion instructions.
- register-lean tile (R4D_LM4_LEAN) and two-tile waves (R4D_LM4_NPW): the u4
  g64 head spills at every row-tile count above one (ScratchSize 68-748 B a
  lane at MT 2-4), the 4.5 ms (MT 3) to 8.3 ms (MT 4) cliff of a c8 decode
  trace. LEAN=1 keeps the scale-group loop rolled: no scratch at any MT, 218-245
  VGPR. NPW=2 shares each activation fragment and the sum-of-x WMMA between two
  weight tiles. Both only reorder issue, not arithmetic (bit-identical).
  LEAN is auto: 1 from MT >= 2 (M > 16), 0 at MT 1 (M <= 16), where the rolled
  loop costs ~10 %; R4D_LM4_LEAN overrides. NPW stays 1 by default.

The rows are selected by the container (the lm_head's encoding), so nothing
changes for an existing container. The auto LEAN level only picks a kernel
variant of the u4 head and is bit-identical to the previous one.

Measured on an R9700 at 210 W, GPTQ-MXFP4 Qwen3.8-27B + DFlash2 k7:
- i4 sym g128 head (logit error 11.2 % RMS; vLLM's int4 head 10.8 %): step
  36.1 -> 35.5 ms, code 131 -> 141 tok/s, story 50.9 -> 53.5, explain
  88.9 -> 90.1.
- u4 g64 head (rtn codes=u4 zero=u8 group=64 scale=bf16 rule=search): weight
  error 0.112 -> 0.089; KL against the fp8-head container (5256 positions,
  code/docs/de) mean 0.0155 -> 0.0057, p99.9 0.260 -> 0.041, top-1 93.7 ->
  95.6 %, PPL x1.012 -> x1.003. Step time unchanged (~35.5 ms).
- nibble trick: logits_gemm_u4g64 1438 -> 1351 us a verify step; KL unchanged.
- lean tile, lm_head u4 g64: M=32 5971 -> 2177 us, M=48 4659 -> 2928 us, M <= 16
  unchanged; c8 decode trace lm_head 4.52 -> 2.62 ms/step, step 55.0 -> 52.1 ms;
  c8 staggered arrivals 405-416 -> 425 tok/s; KL 0.009889.

Tests: r4d_selftest layout, inverse and numerics at M 1/8/33/64/70, K 5120 and
the padded 2560 row; bitwise identity of every NPW x LEAN point against the
default; `--perflm4 N K M [iters]` sweeps FKB x NPW x LEAN. docs/KERNELS.md
lists the three rows under "Rows nothing ran"; docs/GUIDE.md and
libr4d/README.md document the launch pins.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
