From 178d68244cc0e896b8054476c8790a042d8fbbff Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: slydlake <sly.dlake@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 14:50:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 08/16] E4M3 token embedding and DFlash2 selector codebooks
 (embed_lookup_q f32 scale, dflash_select_q)

Two big static tables held at E4M3 under f32 scales, chosen by what the
container says they are, so every existing container is declared and served as
before. The difference goes to the KV cache.

Token embedding. The qwen35 architecture declares the token table and its
scale as an embed_lookup_q operand pair -- for the trunk and for the DFlash2
drafter, which embeds through the target table -- when the container holds
token_embd as fp8_e4m3 under a single scale (recipe: token_embd rtn
codes=fp8_e4m3 block=*x* scale=f32 rule=search, relative error 2.64 %); a bf16
table is served as before. libr4d's embed_lookup_q layout hook now accepts an
f32 scale plane as well as bf16 (the kernel already reads either), which is what
a converted token embedding carries. The table is 1.18 GiB instead of 2.37: at
262144 context, 4 sequences, --max-num-batched-tokens 2048 the pool grows
376384 -> 415200 tokens. Speed unchanged (12 mixed prompts: 33.2-33.4 ms/step;
prefill 10.8k ~2228 tok/s). KL against the fp8-head container: mean 0.0057 ->
0.0099, top-1 95.6 -> 95.1 %, PPL x1.0031 -> x1.0038.

Selector codebooks. sel_pred / sel_succ are 2 x [248320, 256] bf16 = 2 x 121 MiB
of static weights. A container holding them as fp8_e4m3 codes with an f32 scale
a row (recipe: `rtn codes=fp8_e4m3 block=1x* scale=f32`; a scale plane for the
whole table is read too) is served by a new op, dflash_select_q. It is an op of
its own, as embed_lookup_q is: the operand list differs and operands are
positional. One table E4M3 and the other bf16 is refused with a message. About
119 MiB go to the KV cache (~3.8k tokens at fp8 KV); a draft is verified, so
only acceptance can move (seq8-kv A/B at 210 W: KL 0.009874 unchanged).

libr4d: one kernel body templated on the codebook element, row
dflash_select_q_fp8, schema, shape hook. libref: ref_dflash_select_q (one body
for both spellings). libavx: host kernel (avx_check compares it against libref
at two shapes). docs/OPS.md, docs/KERNELS.md.

Tests: r4d_selftest case for dflash_select_q (exact power-of-two data, row scale
and one-scale-for-the-table, bigram form); ref_test op_dflash_select_q with
hand-computed expectations that tell a missing predecessor/successor scale apart.

