From db82e1efda596e1253be22b5a0fae2eb8734c3a9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: slydlake <sly.dlake@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 14:50:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 09/16] DFlash2: 4-bit and int8 draft head, read off the
 container

The drafter proposes from the top K of a coarse copy of the target lm_head
(u2 today). Against the vLLM serve of the same model and drafter, Radiance
accepted fewer tokens a step (1.75 vs 1.85 on a story prompt), and the candidate
set is exactly what the selector has to work with: a coarse head ranks the right
token outside the K it hands on and no later stage recovers it.

- u4 (w4a8_asym): a recipe that writes the head `codes=u4 zero=u8 group=128
  scale=f16` gets libr4d's w4a8_asym GEMM over the same int8 activation and the
  same group sums (~660 MiB instead of ~330). Qwen3.8-27B MXFP4 + DFlash2 on an
  R9700, 512 tokens: story 48.2 -> 52.0 tok/s (292 -> 267 steps, 1.92 tok/step),
  explain 85.3 -> 92.0, code 120.8 -> 121.4; 4 concurrent 138 -> 154 tok/s.
  Prefix caching on or off changes nothing.
- int8 (i8a8): `codes=i8 group=128 scale=bf16 clamp=sym` is served at i8a8
  (quant_act_i8g into a [srows, n_embd/128] f32 scale plane, then gemm_nt_q).
  Code acceptance 4.53 -> 4.65 tok/step against u4, but the doubled head read
  costs ~0.8 ms a step: story/explain -2..4 %, code +0.5 %. Kept as an option;
  u4 stays the recommendation.

Every existing container is declared and served as before (2-bit head).

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
