From 3f8eaf6e4ebf09eef209d8f5f0e899a3d7bd87e2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: slydlake <sly.dlake@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 14:50:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 12/16] Add gemm_mxfp4a8_atiled: A-fragment-tiled MXFP4 prefill
 GEMM (off by default)

gemm_mxfp4a8_atiled reads the E4M3 activation in WMMA-fragment-tiled layout
straight from global memory into the WMMA registers: no sA staging through
LDS, only the folded W tile goes through LDS (9-10 KB, 3 blocks per CU
instead of 2). Ported from SlyBase/vllm-sly-radiance
(radiance_mxfp4_fp8_gemm_atiled), which builds on the ggz14 / StillDeadcode
fragment-tiled kernel. Differences from the source: only the fragment-order
weight, no E6 / partition arms, this tree's kMxtMag table, and the
(row, 128 of K) activation grid carried exactly like the staged kernel
(bit-identical).

Layout contract: an optional `afrag` = T op parameter (docs/OPS.md) on
rmsnorm_quant_fp8, gated_quant_fp8 and the mxfp4a8 gemm_nt_q. At an issue's
M >= T the producers write q fragment-tiled and the GEMM reads it with the
atiled kernel; producer and consumer decide from the same M and T, no state
between them. Architecture side: ActFP8::frag, set on the norm output (h)
and the SwiGLU product (ffn) of qwen35_mxfp4 only when
RADIANCE_MXFP4_ATILED_MIN_M=T (default 0 = off, ops unchanged; documented in
GUIDE section 8). Fp8 consumers of a flagged plane are refused at declare;
the MTP head's wire copies declare row-major ops (and only where the FFN has
an ffn plane, so the MoE build is unaffected). libref implements the
permutation; libavx declares the parameter and refuses a fragment-tiled
plane; gated_had_quant_fp8 does not carry it. Schemas and docs/OPS.md carry
the parameter.

Measured in the source project: +11-16 % prefill over the staged kernel.
Here, served on an R9700 with RADIANCE_MXFP4_ATILED_MIN_M=513, same-window
A/B/A/B: prefill +5.6 % at 2k, +6.2 % at 8k, +6.6 % at 32k, +6.2 % at 64k.

Tests: r4d_selftest mxfp4a8_numeric afrag cases compare atiled against the
staged kernel bitwise (NaN pad rows); producer cases compare the tiled plane
against the row-major run; ref_test op_afrag_layout_round_trips (host).

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
