From: slydlake <sly.dlake@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 14:50:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 13/16] DFlash2: MXFP4 drafter linears

DenseFP8 learns LinearFP8's mx branch without the GEMM. An e2m1/E8M0 weight is
declared as codes, exponent plane and reference view; gemm()/bref() give a block
the matching gemm_nt_q (fp8a8 or mxfp4a8) and its trailing b_ref operand.
rad_block_dflash2.h declares its nine GEMMs through gemm() and issues bref();
the gated gate_up fold (an fp8a8 tile) is skipped for an MXFP4 gate_up. The
format is read off the container, so every existing container is declared and
served as before.

Measured with a GPTQ-MXFP4 Qwen3.8-27B + DFlash2 on an R9700, 512 tokens,
story/code/explain tok/s: fp8 drafter 48.2/121/85.4, all-MXFP4 50.0/115.7/85.3,
hybrid (FFN and fc only) 48.7/121/84.4. The drafter's GEMMs drop from ~3.4 to
~2.1 ms a step, but RTN to MXFP4 (11.7 % relative error vs 2.6 % for fp8) costs
acceptance on code; a calibrated drafter would keep it. A draft is verified, so
only acceptance can move. Not the recommended recipe; an option.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
