Subject: [PATCH 14/16] libr4d: tune infrastructure for the MXFP4 GEMM bands
 (wide decode form, edge row, bands test)

The 256-row tiled block serves every M above 64, so a 70-200 token arrival
(MIXED step or short prefill) pays for rows nobody asked for, and decode steps
at concurrency run M = n_seq x 8 where the single (8,64] key is too coarse.

- gemm_mxfp4a8_decode gets a WIDE form (DTM 6/8/12/16, bk 64, split-K 1/2/4,
  partial in the op scratch), reachable only through the tiled row's new
  tune axis dec=1 (+ ks/bk/nt): the selector ranks rows by priority only, so
  the choice has to live in an axis. r4d_tune_valid_mxfp4_tiled refuses dec=1
  above M=256 / N=36864; the tiled scratch hook sizes the partial only for
  dec=1. Defaults unchanged: dec=0 launches the tiled kernel as before, the
  decode row (M<=64) is untouched.
- gemm_nt_q tune bands at M 16/32/48 (decode batch), 128/256/512 and
  1024/2048 (full-batch prefill): (8,64] becomes (8,16] (16,32] (32,48]
  (48,64], the tiled row sees (64,128] (128,256] (256,512] (512,1024]
  (1024,2048] and the rest as separate tune keys (core/plugin/bands.cpp
  collects every LE/GE/EQ of the op). The ks/bk/tn defaults run on the actual
  M, so a band without a tune line launches as before.
- The edges sit on an inert row, gemm_nt_q_bands: priority 0, dtype
  "__bands__" (matches no tensor), launch refuses with RAD_E_UNSUPPORTED.
  Constraints of a row are AND-ed and bands.cpp resolves each band at its
  upper bound, so edges placed on the decode row itself narrowed it to M<=16
  and pushed M 17..64 onto another kernel (GEMM per step 35 -> 122 ms at
  M=32, c8 385 -> 177 tok/s).
- tests/r4d_bands_test reads the real row table from libr4d.so (host only) and
  checks the band list, that the decode row resolves every M<=64, and that the
  edge row is never selected; it prints the row chosen per band.
- r4d_selftest: M=65..256 cases for the tiled row (tn 2/4, both activation
  grids), dec=1 at the same M with ks 1/2/4 and nt 0/1, and the band edges
  65/80/129/193/255 with K=576 and bk=128 requested.

A dec=1 tune line is refused where the A plane can be fragment-tiled: the wide
decode form reads a row-major activation; with RADIANCE_MXFP4_ATILED_MIN_M = T
the producers write it fragment-tiled from M >= T and only the atiled kernel
reads that. The tiled row's tune_valid refuses dec=1 when the geometry carries
afrag > 0 and afrag <= M (M is the band upper bound), which resolve() applies to
cached and pinned lines alike: such a band runs the tiled/atiled kernel. Without
afrag, or with T > 256, nothing changes. tune lines are specific to the T they
were produced with (afrag is part of the gemm_nt_q tune key).
Test: r4d_bands_test tiled_row_refuses_wide_form_with_fragment_plane (host only,
needs RAD_R4D_SO pointing at a libr4d.so; skips without).

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
