From bb7d33fa9a6781dbaef51d29c3a73c59fee74cd4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: slydlake <sly.dlake@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 14:50:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 15/16] libr4d: gemm_nt_q_gated_mx, MXFP4 gate_up + SwiGLU +
 E4M3 quant fold (RADIANCE_MXFP4_GATED_FOLD)

New private op gemm_nt_q_gated_mx and row gemm_mxfp4a8_gated_decode, the MXFP4
twin of gemm_nt_q_gated: one block per 128 fused columns, wave w streams gate
fragment w and up fragment w, and SwiGLU and the quantiser run on the
accumulators. Removes the gated_quant_fp8 launch (and the drafter's silu_mul
plus quantiser) and the bf16 [M, 2n] round trip on the decode band (M <= 64).

Same K order as gemm_mxfp4a8_decode at ks=1 and the same epilogue arithmetic
as gated_quant_fp8, so the result is byte-identical to the pair by
construction (r4d_selftest compares with memcmp). The fold has no split-K, so
it is only declared where the decode GEMM itself runs unsplit: M <= 64 and
2*n_ff >= 14080, which every shipped model satisfies. Architecture side:
MlpFP8 and the DFlash2 drafter declare it beside the pair when
RADIANCE_MXFP4_GATED_FOLD=1 (default off, read at declare time; GUIDE
section 8). libref has no MXFP4 grid, so like dequant_w4 the op is libr4d's
own; docs/OPS.md describes it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
